>
    <p>An estate plan is a set of instructions for the two moments a family is least able to improvise: when someone can no longer make their own decisions, and when they have died. We write those instructions with you, in your words where we can, and make sure they are signed, witnessed and kept where they will be found.</p>
    <p>When the moment comes, we help the people left to carry the plan out. Probate is a process, not a mystery; executors who understand each step make better decisions and fewer expensive ones. Our first meeting with an executor ends with a written list of what happens next, in order.</p>
